@module flutter-m11 | Packages and Dependencies
@summary Find, add, constrain, maintain and create packages and plugins.

@lesson flutter-m11-l01 | pubspec.yaml | 8
## Learning objectives
- Read and edit the project manifest

## pubspec.yaml
pubspec.yaml declares the app name, version (`1.2.0+5`: version name + build number), SDK constraint, dependencies, assets and fonts.

```dart
// version: 1.2.0+5   → versionName 1.2.0, versionCode 5
// environment:
//   sdk: ^3.7.0
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- version holds name+build number.

@lesson flutter-m11-l02 | pub.dev | 8
## Learning objectives
- Evaluate packages before adding them

## pub.dev
On pub.dev check likes, pub points, popularity, the publisher (verified badge), platform support, last update and open issues before depending on a package.

```dart
// Prefer packages from verified publishers such as dart.dev, flutter.dev, google.dev
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Evaluate quality and maintenance first.

@lesson flutter-m11-l03 | Installing packages | 8
## Learning objectives
- Add dependencies with flutter pub add

## Installing packages
`flutter pub add http` adds the latest compatible version to pubspec.yaml and runs pub get. Import it with `package:http/http.dart`.

```dart
import 'package:http/http.dart' as http;

Future<int> ping() async => (await http.get(Uri.parse('https://example.com'))).statusCode;
```

## Summary
- Use flutter pub add; avoid hand-editing versions.

@lesson flutter-m11-l04 | Dependency constraints | 8
## Learning objectives
- Write sensible version constraints

## Dependency constraints
Use caret constraints (`^1.2.0`). Avoid `any`. Use `dependency_overrides` only temporarily to resolve conflicts.

```dart
// dependencies:
//   http: ^1.2.0      # >=1.2.0 <2.0.0
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Caret constraints allow compatible updates.

@lesson flutter-m11-l05 | Semantic versioning | 8
## Learning objectives
- Interpret version numbers

## Semantic versioning
MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH: breaking changes bump MAJOR, features bump MINOR, fixes bump PATCH. Read the CHANGELOG before major upgrades.

```dart
bool isBreaking(String from, String to) => from.split('.').first != to.split('.').first;
void main() => print(isBreaking('1.4.0', '2.0.0'));
```

## Summary
- Major bumps may break your code.

@lesson flutter-m11-l06 | Dependency conflicts | 8
## Learning objectives
- Resolve version solving failures

## Dependency conflicts
If two packages need incompatible versions of a third, pub fails. Upgrade both, check `flutter pub deps`, or temporarily override.

```dart
// flutter pub outdated
// flutter pub deps --style=compact
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Inspect the graph, then upgrade.

@lesson flutter-m11-l07 | Flutter plugins | 8
## Learning objectives
- Understand packages with native code

## Flutter plugins
Plugins contain Dart plus Kotlin/Swift code (camera, location). They require a full rebuild and sometimes native configuration such as permissions.

```dart
import 'package:url_launcher/url_launcher.dart';

Future<bool> openDocs() => launchUrl(Uri.parse('https://docs.flutter.dev'));
```

## Summary
- Plugins need a full rebuild after adding.

@lesson flutter-m11-l08 | Platform packages | 8
## Learning objectives
- Handle platform-specific support

## Platform packages
Check each package's supported platforms. Use `kIsWeb` and `defaultTargetPlatform` to branch when a feature isn't available everywhere.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/foundation.dart';

bool get supportsFiles => !kIsWeb;
```

## Summary
- Guard features per platform.

@lesson flutter-m11-l09 | Creating packages | 8
## Learning objectives
- Share code as a package

## Creating packages
`flutter create --template=package my_widgets` creates a reusable package; `--template=plugin` creates a plugin with native code.

```dart
// flutter create --template=package bimo_widgets
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Packages share Dart code; plugins add native code.

@lesson flutter-m11-l10 | Maintaining dependencies | 8
## Learning objectives
- Keep dependencies healthy

## Maintaining dependencies
Run `flutter pub outdated` regularly, upgrade in small steps, run tests after each upgrade and remove unused packages.

```dart
// flutter pub upgrade --major-versions (review changes!)
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Small, frequent upgrades are safest.

@lesson flutter-m11-l11 | Common useful packages | 8
## Learning objectives
- Know the popular essentials

## Common useful packages
Frequently used: go_router (navigation), provider/flutter_riverpod/flutter_bloc (state), http/dio (network), shared_preferences, sqflite/drift (storage), intl (formatting), cached_network_image, url_launcher, path_provider.

```dart
import 'package:intl/intl.dart';

String price(double v) => NumberFormat.currency(symbol: '\$').format(v);
```

## Summary
- Lean on well-maintained packages.
